### Page 1 of 48

```text
MEMORANDUM
TO:
The Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins and City of Cheyenne Council Members
FROM:
Robin Lockman, City Treasurer
DATE:
May 3, 2023
SUBJECT:
Wyoming CLASS Investment Pool Resolution
On May 8, 2023, the Governing Body will be referring a resolution to the Finance Committee that
would authorize the City to become a participant in the Wyoming Cooperative Liquid Assets
Securities System (Wyoming CLASS).
Wyoming CLASS is an investment pool that allows the state of Wyoming and its political
subdivisions to participate.  This includes any county, city, town, school district, community
college district, hospital district, and special district.  Current participants include 18 Wyoming
counties as well as several municipalities and special districts throughout the state.  Some of the
larger municipality participants include the cities of Rock Springs, Green River, Douglas, Gillette,
Cody, and Riverton. Evanston and Laramie County should also become participants soon.
Wyoming CLASS is rated “AAAm” by S&P Global Ratings Services, the highest rating assigned
to principal stability government investment pools.  This rating reflects the conservative nature of
the pool’s investments, as well as the excellent credit quality of the program.  Wyoming CLASS
invests solely in securities that are permitted by Wyoming State Law and adheres to the
requirements of the City of Cheyenne’s Investment Policy Statement.
Wyoming CLASS currently is the highest yielding of the three local government investment pools
in the state.  Their current 7-day yield is 4.8894%.  In comparison, the Wyoming
Government Investment Fund (WGIF), in which the City is a participant, has a 7-day yield of
4.75%.  Wyo-Star I, through the Wyoming State Treasurer’s Office, had a current yield of
3.6616% as of March 31, 2023, which is the last statement I have received.
Investments made on behalf of the participants are subject to the overall direction of the Wyoming
CLASS Board of Trustees.  Members include Bill Novotny, Johnson County Commissioner; Katie
Smits, Teton County Treasurer; Matt McBurnett, City of Rock Springs Administrative Services
Director; Michelle Henderson, City of Gillette Finance Director; and Kelli Little, Executive
Director of the Wyoming Association of Conservation Districts.  Their legal counsel is Pat Crank.
As always, if you have any questions, please give me a call at 637-6336 or email at
rlockman@cheyennecity.org.
```

### Page 2 of 48

```text
RESOLUTION NO. _____________

ENTITLED: "A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING THE CITY OF CHEYENNE TO JOIN
WITH OTHER POLITICAL SUBDIVISIONS OF THE STATE OF
WYOMING AS A PARTICIPANT IN THE WYOMING COOPERATIVE
LIQUID ASSETS SECURITIES SYSTEM (Wyoming CLASS) TO POOL
FUNDS FOR INVESTMENT."

WHEREAS, Wyoming Statute § 9-4-831 authorizes political subdivisions of the State of
Wyoming, including municipalities (Political Subdivisions), to invest in eligible securities as
specified by statute ("Legal Investments");

WHEREAS, under Wyoming Statute § 9-4-831(a)(viii), Political Subdivisions may
invest jointly with other investors in a commingled fund of Legal Investments;

WHEREAS, the Wyoming Cooperative Liquid Assets Securities System (Wyoming
CLASS or the Trust) was organized in 2020 pursuant to the laws of the state of Wyoming and
provides a convenient method for Political Subdivisions to pool their liquid assets collectively;

WHEREAS, the Trust is a professionally managed local government investment pool
trust fund available only to political subdivisions in Wyoming. The Trust seeks a high level of
current income consistent with the preservation of capital and maintenance of liquidity;

WHEREAS, U.S. Bank National Association serves as the custodian for the Trust (the
Custodian) and all eligible securities of the Trust are held through the Custodian;

WHEREAS, the Custodian does not participate in the Trust’s investment
decision-making process but acts as safekeeping agent for the Trust’s investment portfolios and
serves, in accordance with Wyoming Statute, as the depository in connection with the direct
investment and withdrawal mechanisms of the Trust;

WHEREAS, it is the interest of the participating Political Subdivisions to permit their
respective cash balances to be invested in the Trust because the Trust offers a reasonably safe,
liquid, and competitive investment option; and

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne desires to become a participant in the Trust and has
determined the City Treasurer should be appointed as the Key Contact through which all official
communications between the Trust and the City of Cheyenne will be conducted.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the City of Cheyenne hereby approves, adopts, and
thereby joins as a participant with other Political Subdivisions pursuant to the Wyoming CLASS
Indenture of Trust dated May 29, 2020, as amended from time-to-time, the terms of which are
incorporated herein by this reference and a copy of which shall be filed with the minutes of the
meeting at which this Resolution is adopted;

9:11 am, May 02, 2023
```

